per-engine.broiler-js: error: RangeError
per-engine.broiler-vm: error: RangeError
divergence.broiler-js: BigInt.asUintN converts a width of 2^32 or more to a 32-bit integer, so the modulus is wrong, giving a wrong value, or zero, raising a .NET DivideByZeroException, where the result of a negative value is past any representation and a RangeError. Answered by Broiler.JS docs/roadmap/SharedLibraries.md, SJL-4.5 (the correction of asUintN at very large widths).
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-bigint.asuintn ref:numericsref@1
script: BigInt.asUintN(4294967296, (-1n)) > 0n
note: a value of 4294967296 bits: out holds the specification's answer; the specification's value cannot be represented by any engine; each plan answers a RangeError at its representation's limit (JSD-0067 decision 2, Broiler.JS SharedLibraries.md SJL-4.5)
